# ── DOCS IMAGERY LIVES LOCALLY, NOT IN THE REPO ──────────────────────────────
# Every bug report, lookdev frame and reference sheet is a 2–5 MB PNG, and 268
# of them made the tracked tree 405 MB — 361 MB of it these. That is what a
# clone pays, what a CI checkout shuffles, and why the free-tier runner is
# expensive. Keep shooting them, keep them on disk, keep referencing them from
# SPEC.md and docs/*.md by path — just do not commit them.
#
# NOTE: this stops the BLEEDING, it does not undo it. The 395 MB already in
# history stays there until someone rewrites it (filter-repo + force push),
# which is a separate, destructive decision. A shallow CI checkout (the
# default) never fetches that history, so this alone fixes the CI cost.
docs/**/*.png
docs/**/*.jpg
docs/**/*.jpeg
docs/**/*.gif
docs/**/*.webp
docs/**/*.mp4
docs/**/*.mov
